Faultlens 1.0 Debian package
==================================

Run `faultlens` as your ordinary user to open the terminal workspace.
`tui` remains an alias. Explicit CLI examples:

    faultlens status
    faultlens health
    faultlens investigate --mode now
    faultlens --help

The package requires system Python >= 3.11 and includes the reviewed Textual
frontend and its private pure-Python dependencies. No virtual environment or pip
setup is needed on the server. Private libraries are updated by rebuilding and
upgrading Faultlens, not by installing distribution Textual packages.

No Faultlens daemon, recording service, log policy or extra permission is installed.
Optional tools such as Atop require a separate administrator decision. Existing
permissions and retained evidence determine which diagnostics are available.

User preferences and evidence are outside package ownership and survive removal.
The source/wheel SHA-256 manifest is in build-manifest.json; complete upstream
licenses remain in /usr/share/faultlens/vendor/*.dist-info/ and LICENSE contains
Faultlens's GPL text. Source and build instructions:
https://github.com/mfuryto/faultlens

Release assets include matching source, dependency wheels and checksums. Isolated
Debian/Ubuntu installation tests do not replace the unavailable second real-server
SSH test. Security reports use the private GitHub advisory route in SECURITY.md.
